    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19743" root="سطع" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُسَطَّعٌ</span></b>  (assumed tropical:)  A camel <i>marked with the mark called</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِطَاع</span>; (S, TA;) fem. with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span>. and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَسْطُوعَةٌ</span></b> 
signifies the same, applied to a she-camel. (TA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِبِلٌ مُسَطَّعَةٌ</span> (assumed tropical:)  <i>Camels tall as the tent-poles
called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُطُعٌ</span>, pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِطَاعٌ</span>. (TA.)

